<h1>Learning The Basics</h1>
<p>Get a feel for Quickfire without diving into every setting. This is the tour that helps you feel at home.</p>
<div class="image-placeholder">Add a friendly collage showing the homepage, search bar, and a client record.</div>
<h2>Start on Home</h2>
<p>Home shows your tasks, renewals, and quick tiles for proposals, certs, and payments. It is the daily launchpad, not a one-time setup screen.</p>
<h2>Search from anywhere</h2>
<p>Use the FireSearch bar to jump to clients, policies, and documents. Type a few letters, arrow down, and press Enter. It is the fastest way to move without memorizing menus.</p>
<div class="image-placeholder">Add an animation of the search box being used to find a client.</div>
<h2>Open a client and explore</h2>
<p>Inside a client record you see contacts, policies, tasks, and files in one place. Attach forms, log a call, or send a template without switching tabs.</p>
<h2>Use the chat panel when you need help</h2>
<p>Keep the help pane open while you work. Switch to Staff chat for quick internal questions or SMS to text a client, all while the record stays in view.</p>
<div class="image-placeholder">Add a side-by-side of the client record on the left and chat/help panel on the right.</div>
<h2>Templates and agents do the heavy lifting</h2>
<p>Templates fill common emails so you do not rewrite them. Agents run small workflows tailored to the page you are on. Lean on them to handle repeat steps.</p>
<h2>When something feels off</h2>
<p>Refresh this panel, check Troubleshooting, or ping support with what you were doing. You do not have to spend long on fixes.</p>
